  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.09,
      "text": "One of my favorite things about being an epidemiologist is just the variety to the job."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.09,
      "end": 12.03,
      "text": "There's never a boring day, and really being able to go after those answers to research questions."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.03,
      "end": 15.77,
      "text": "That I myself can go out and try to find the answers."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.77,
      "end": 17.95,
      "text": "And I absolutely love my job."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.95,
      "end": 21.1,
      "text": "I feel like I'm doing a good thing."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.1,
      "end": 23.4,
      "text": "I'm impacting, potentially, workers' lives."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.4,
      "end": 25.67,
      "text": "There's just no price you can put on that."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.95,
      "end": 31.08,
      "text": "My mother works at NIOSH and has been there since I was a young child."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.52,
      "end": 39.61,
      "text": "My mom brought me in for mother-daughter day probably in my mid-teens, and I got to see what epidemiologists do and I got to hang out"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.61,
      "end": 43.83,
      "text": "with industrial hygienists and other researchers and kind of see what they do."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.39,
      "end": 45.89,
      "text": "That was sort of my first introduction."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.02,
      "end": 47.2,
      "text": "I never expected to be in epidemiology."
    }
  ],
